A||N||8||DreXteR||Crazy Fuel Gauge||||1||
Z||000000||DreXteR||09-08-2000||01:22 AM||||Hi all, I bought my fiero about a month.  And don’t drive it yet, 'til I fix all things(I want to reconstruct it the perfect way). Well, the car is not wrecked, but have some little stuff to fix.  <P>The Problem: The fuel gauge readings are bad.  Lets me explain, instead display full or any other amount in the tank, it display to top right, super above the full line in the gauge.<P>So, I think the problem could be the gauge, but now I don’t think so. Here is the crazy stuff, if I shake the car the gauge start to move left and right, so I continue doing it and the gauge now points to the true gas level. But if I shake the car again, then it gets back to the far right off gas scale.<P>Solution: Well, I think the problem resides in the fuel-sending unit.  I will have to take down the tank and take it out. The big prize question....<P>Somebody has open the fuel sending unit and fix it or have some knowledge in how I can fix it?<P>Thanx for the help.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||09-08-2000||01:58 AM||||The problem could be the gage. The glue that holds the needle to the spindle breaks down and the needle is loose. You can CAREFULLY remove needle and glue it into place, (where you know the needle should point with ignition on) <BR>If you think it's the sending unit check the eletrical connections before dropping the tank. A little corrosion can make the gages freak out. That includes the dash connectors too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||RossT||09-08-2000||07:33 AM||||This is a common problem with fieros. Alot of people on the forum have run out of gas with the gauge showing 1/4 full!! Most of the time it is the sending unit.  Ray Paulk has written an article about how to recalibrate the sending unit, but you have to drop the tank to do this.  Most people simply fill the gas tank so it full, pull the needle of and put it back on with needle showing full (cause the tank is full).  The gt i recently bought does the same thing.  The needle pegs all the way to the right.  I am going to readjust the needle.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||09-08-2000||07:54 AM||||I've got a problem with my gauge as well. However, my problem is a little different. The gauge never reads full even though I know it is, and never reads less than a 1/4 tank, even though I start to hear the fuel pump wine. Sending unit or loose needle?<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000004||stsmithgt||09-08-2000||12:58 PM||||I had a fuel gauge problem when my fuel pump was going bad.  I had the fuel pump replaced and the symptoms the gauge had went away.  They said the pump was drawing so much energy because it was burning out that it was interfering with the readings the fuel gauge was giving. That's my two cents <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000005||DreXteR||09-08-2000||01:45 PM||||stsmigthgt-<BR>Who I know in the conditions of my fuel pump?<P>RussT-<BR>I cant find the article from Ray Paulk. Can u give me the direct link?  Maybe its a dirty conector, the alternator was giving me a low volt reading(like 9 to 11 volts), I take off all the wires clean it and Voalaa!!  Now its like 13.5. For sure the will be some similar problems in the car.<P>Another thing I forgot to mention is whe I shake the car the temp sensor moves too but the needle returns to the position was before.<P>I take off the fuel gauge and verify-clean it, and I dont think the needle its loose.  I rotate it with my finger and it move with a little restriction, so the needle its well placed in the gauge. Another test was hitting the dash with my hand( not so hard that I can broke it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) and the needle was firmly poniting to the far right. <P>Im dieing to ride it!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <BR>But I have to wait til finish repair all the gizmos problems. Sorry, but Im the kind of people that like to do things the right way. Anyway, its better 4 the car 2  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I like this baby a lot! I have looking 4 one about 2 years, and finally find one in good conditions. This is my second car, my dalily drive car is a Gran Vitara 99, and can smoke those v6 mostangs like tiny-wini. hehehe<P>I want fix any ****  in the fiero(gt 86 4spd) to make it like new, then place all performance goodies I can get  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>I will like to see all those v8 guys face when my baby take them in to shame.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>Well, Thanx 4 da help. I will continue in my saga to restore my little baby, besides I will keep it til GOD call 4 me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> heheeh. Its good to have a place like this to solves problems.<P>Long live 2 the Little Giant Killer!!!<P>DreXteR!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||RossT||09-08-2000||02:50 PM||||Here is the Ray Paulk link. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.mn.org/Knowledge/Procedure.asp?Version=w6x2v73u&Catid=22&Id=46&Action=Edit" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.mn.org/Knowledge/Procedure.asp?Version=w6x2v73u&Catid=22&Id=46&Act   ion=Edit</A> <P>good info posted by the Minnesota Fiero Club<BR>in their tech section.<P>you can also find tech info on just about anything at: <A HREF="http://www.fco.org/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fco.org/index.html</A> <P>click on service guide!!!<P>Ross<P>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 09-08-2000).]<P>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 09-08-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 09-08-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||09-08-2000||04:56 PM||||Sounds like it's the wire to the sender. The tank can move a bit in the brackets and pinch/break the wire. Could be the sender itself, plenty of those are batty around here. I don't think it's the gauge<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||DreXteR||09-09-2000||11:54 AM||||Thax RossT 4 da link. I will check it l8tr, my fiace is on da way here and we are going to Penny and Sears.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Theogre<BR>I will check that too, but whe someone came here, alone its a super diff think to do alone. Move wires and look at the gauge @ same time ...heheh  Well, I was thinking why if  the car is shaked the fuel gauge start moving, and the reasonable explenation is when the gas in the tank is being moved(by shaking the car) it can move the sending unit in dif directions make it in a certain way working right. That make me think that the have some mis-contact in the sending unit, maybe for age or wear. The real thing is that I think can the sending unit can be fixed. And less money sepended.  eheheheh<BR>Im in a bad economical situation 'cause bougth the car. My weading will be in Dicember and are expensives  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> then aperars the car, the 1 I was looking 4, was a now or never deal(not by price, here in PR there only a few fieros in good conditions) I fall in love with it and WTF!!  Ask my dad 4 some loan and get it.  <P>Well, 1st I have to pay my dad the money, the can buy the parts needed for the car.  Meanwhile I will fix all I can without spending money or a lil bit of it.<P>Thaks foe the help!!<P>||||reg||10
